{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "i recently watched \"the social network\" and was thoroughly impressed by the film's thought-provoking themes, engaging storyline, and exceptional cinematography. directed by david fincher, the movie tells the story of mark zuckerberg, the founder of facebook, and the consequences of his success.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, a sophomore at harvard university, being dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright, played by rachel morgan. this event sparks mark's idea to create a website called \"facemash,\" which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes an instant hit, but also gets mark into trouble with the university administration.\n\nmark then teams up with his college roommates, eduardo saverin, played by andrew garfield, and the twins cameron and tyler winklevoss, played by armie hammer, to create a new website called \"thefacebook.\" the site quickly gains popularity, and mark becomes a sensation on campus.\n\nas the film progresses, it becomes clear that mark's success is not without its costs. he becomes increasingly isolated and withdrawn, and his relationships with his friends and family begin to suffer. eduardo, in particular, feels betrayed by mark's actions, and the two become embroiled in a bitter dispute over the ownership and direction of facebook.\n\none of the standout aspects of \"the social network\" is its exploration of the themes of ambition, greed, and the consequences of success. mark zuckerberg is portrayed as a complex and multifaceted character, driven by a desire for recognition and validation. his relentless pursuit of success ultimately leads to his downfall, as he sacrifices his relationships and his integrity in the process.\n\nthe film's cinematography is also noteworthy, with a distinctive and stylish visual aesthetic that captures the mood and atmosphere of the characters and their world. the use of lighting, camera angles, and composition all contribute to a sense of tension and unease, underscoring the film's themes of conflict and betrayal.\n\nthe performances in \"the social network\" are also exceptional, with jesse eisenberg delivering a nuanced and compelling portrayal of mark zuckerberg. andrew garfield is equally impressive as eduardo saverin, bringing a sense of vulnerability and sensitivity to the role. the supporting cast, including justin timberlake as sean parker, the co-founder of napster, and brenda song as christy lee, add to the film's depth and complexity.\n\noverall, \"the social network\" is a thought-provoking and engaging film that offers a fascinating glimpse into the world of mark zuckerberg and the creation of facebook. with its exceptional cinematography, outstanding performances, and nuanced exploration of themes, it is a must-see for anyone interested in the story behind one of the world's most influential companies.", "logprobs": [{"token": "i", "logprob": -1.700076699256897}, {"token": " recently", "logprob": -0.015175011940300465}, {"token": " watched", "logprob": -0.07889139652252197}, {"token": " \"", "logprob": -0.0025484247598797083}, {"token": "the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " social", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.011047743260860443}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.011054816655814648}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.2195601910352707}, {"token": " thoroughly", "logprob": -0.0015235256869345903}, {"token": " impressed", "logprob": -3.397406908334233e-05}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.0015026956098154187}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.004123637918382883}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0009801351698115468}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -4.541770613286644e-05}, {"token": " thought", "logprob": -1.0995607376098633}, {"token": "-prov", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "okin